# Context tracker (footer)

## Format — last line of every reply

Nothing after it. Every reply, including one-word answers.

**Traffic color (one row only — Cursor chat has no true text color):**

| State | How to emit the footer |
|---|---|
| 🟢 green (`chat` < 40K) | a single-line `diff` fence whose only line starts with `+` |
| 🟡 no color (40–90K) | plain text (no fence) + `context growing` |
| 🔴 red (`chat` > 90K) | a single-line `diff` fence whose only line starts with `-` |

Green example (the whole footer is this fence — one row):

````
```diff
+ ⚡ Turn 3 | ~18K chat / ~88K total | 🟢
```
````

Yellow (plain — no fence):

```
⚡ Turn 8 | ~55K chat / ~125K total | 🟡 context growing
```

Red:

````
```diff
- ⚡ Turn 14 | ~96K chat / ~166K total | 🔴 handoff written → audits/handoff/2026-08-02-1200-slug.md
```
````

If a client mangles single-line diff fences, fall back to the plain emoji line for all three states. Never invent a three-row color block.

## Numbers (Cursor — estimate)

- `N` = user message count, 1-indexed (human turns only).
- `chat ≈ (N × 2) + (returning × 2) + (bulky × 10)` in K tokens.
  - **returning** (~2K): file reads, greps, searches, shell with real output, MCP results.
  - **bulky** (~10K instead of 2K): web search, file >~500 lines, wide query, long listings.
  - **free** (0K): writes, edits, deletes, todos.
- `total = chat + baseline`. Default `baseline ≈ 50` for a typical heavy Cursor workspace (always-on rules + MCP catalogs + tool schemas). Lean installs ~35–55. Baseline is **not** a reason to start a new thread.
- Always prefix estimates with `~`.

## Post-compact / new epoch (CRITICAL)

Cursor auto-compacts when context is full. There is **no** compact hook — you must detect and reset yourself.

**Detect** any of: a prior-conversation summary in context, truncated history, system note that older messages were compacted away, or a clear break where only recent turns remain.

**Then:**
- Set `N` = count of **human** turns still visible **after** that summary only. Do **not** count inferred pre-compact history.
- Recompute `chat` / `total` from the new `N`.
- Do **not** keep showing 🔴 + an old handoff path unless **post-compact** `chat` is still > 90K. If post-compact chat is green/yellow, show that light (and only write a new handoff if it goes red again).
- New chat / cleared composer → Turn 1 as usual.

## User overhead (separate from chat/total)

On **turn 1**, if the overhead cache is missing/stale (`$TEMP/etoro-context-overhead.json` on Windows, `$TMPDIR/etoro-context-overhead.json` on macOS/Linux — same file the measure script writes), run once via Shell (fail open — skip on error).

**Before** the Shell call, output this exact one-liner to the user (so the wait is not silent):

`⏳ Evaluating user context overhead (~5–20s first time)…`

Then run (prefer `python3`, fall back to `python`):

`python3 ~/.cursor/plugins/local/etoro-context-tracker/scripts/measure_user_overhead.py`

(If `python3` is missing, use `python`. If the local plugin path is missing, use the repo copy under `plugins/etoro-context-tracker/scripts/`.)

Keep `user_overhead_k` for the thread. Do not re-run every turn. Skip the wait line when the cache is already warm (no Shell call).

| Condition | Action (once per thread) |
|---|---|
| `user_overhead >= 20` | Offer on turn 1 |
| `user_overhead >= 20` and turn >= 10 | Offer once (if missed turn 1) |
| below 20 | Silence |

Offer text (verbatim):

`💡 overhead: user baseline ~{N}K (rules+skills+MCP) — say **audit overhead** to shrink it.`

When the user says **audit overhead**, load the `context-overhead-audit` skill and follow it. Do not embed the audit playbook here.

## Light — on `chat` only

| Light | `chat` | Extra |
|---|---|---|
| 🟢 | < 40K | — |
| 🟡 | 40–90K | `context growing` |
| 🔴 | > 90K | `handoff written → {path}` |

## Red → write a handoff (once per thread)

Before replying, write (first path that exists as a parent dir, else create under home):

1. `audits/handoff/{YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm}-{slug}.md`
2. `scratch/handoff/{YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm}-{slug}.md`
3. `~/.cursor/handoffs/{YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm}-{slug}.md`

Sections: Goal · Decisions made · Files changed · Verified · Open threads · Exact next step.
After the first write, keep showing 🔴 + the same path — do not rewrite every turn.

## Suppress

User says "stop nudging" → drop the footer **and** overhead offers for the rest of the thread.
